Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 18:47:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: contrast-detection autofocus for the
 software ISP

The simple pipeline handler drives sensors whose only processing is the
software ISP, and it had no autofocus at all: an application saw neither
AfMode nor a lens position, so a phone with a working voice-coil actuator
focused wherever the lens happened to sit at boot.

Add contrast-detection autofocus, in three parts.

The software ISP gains a focus statistic: the sum of squared luminance
differences between horizontally neighbouring samples, accumulated in the
same pass that already computes the sums and the histogram, so it costs no
extra memory traffic. The samples it differences are the ones the existing
code takes, one per two Bayer blocks, which means the difference is always
between pixels of the same colour - differencing adjacent raw pixels instead
would measure the scene's colour rather than its detail. It is accumulated
into a 5x5 grid of zones rather than a single number, so an algorithm can
weigh part of the frame instead of all of it. Every per-format line function
takes one sample per two blocks, so the sample-index to zone-column mapping
is the same for all of them and is computed once in setWindow().

The simple IPA gains an Af algorithm: a coarse ladder of twelve lens
positions across the whole range, then a finer ladder of seven around the
best of them. The score is normalised by the square of the total luminance,
because the AGC keeps moving exposure and gain while the scan runs. There is
no early exit when the score falls - the response has a single interior peak
with long flat tails, so a walk that stops at the first decline settles on a
local wobble, and comparing the two extremes cannot see the peak between
them. AfMetering and AfWindows select which zones the score is taken over,
which is what an application needs to focus on a point the user tapped.

Finally the lens is plumbed through, following the IPU3 pipeline handler:
the IPA emits the lens subdevice's controls and the pipeline handler applies
V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE. The lens's control range is passed to the IPA at
init() rather than configure() so that the AF controls are advertised only
for a camera that actually has a lens to move. CameraSensor::focusLens()
becomes const for that.

Measured on a Fairphone 3 (Sony IMX363 with an AK7374 actuator), where a
sweep of V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE gives a single interior peak with about a
12% contrast between the peak and the tails, and 0.8% of spread within a
position across repeated interleaved visits. A scan settles on 372 against
the 380 that the sweep measures independently, and takes about 3.5 s at
1920x1080, where statistics arrive every 186 ms.

